{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-05_08-31-36-etcd_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A1: a leader assigns term/index to proposals, appends unstable entries and replicates through peer Progress. Local and remote append support is published after persistence. Responses pass term dispatch and known-peer checks, update Match and contribute only through current configured voter majorities; joint commitment is the minimum of the two majority-supported indexes. maybeCommit advances only when that index has current term. Advancement broadcasts to followers; matching append constrains follower commit to received prefix, heartbeat producer caps it by peer Match, and committed conflicts cannot overwrite history. Ready exposes committed entries with applying cursor and size controls; caller applies configurations and state-machine entries, then completion updates applied. Rejected appends backtrack; heartbeat responses reopen flow and snapshots catch up compacted peers.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-form\",\n        \"B-follower\",\n        \"B-io\",\n        \"B-apply\",\n        \"B-recover\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-commit\",\n        \"F-applied\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-advance\",\n        \"S-application\",\n        \"S-async\",\n        \"S-caller\",\n        \"S-config-restore\",\n        \"S-dispatch\",\n        \"S-durable\",\n        \"S-follower\",\n        \"S-init\",\n        \"S-joint\",\n        \"S-load\",\n        \"S-log-apply\",\n        \"S-log-core\",\n        \"S-log-pointers\",\n        \"S-log-qualification\",\n        \"S-majority\",\n        \"S-node-loop\",\n        \"S-proposal\",\n        \"S-ready\",\n        \"S-ready-build\",\n        \"S-replication\",\n        \"S-restore\",\n        \"S-send\",\n        \"S-storage\",\n        \"S-storage-resp\",\n        \"S-tracker\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A2: eligible voters campaign only without unapplied committed configuration or pending snapshot. Real campaign increments term, records self vote durably and requests votes using last log term/index; configured majority votes acquire leadership. Pre-vote preserves local term until its quorum succeeds. Leader acquisition resets volatile support and appends a current-term empty entry. Higher terms normally step down with lease/pre-vote exceptions; old replies are discarded. Quorum loss can step down; transfer selects a caught-up voter, drops proposals while active and expires after electionTimeout if still leader. Restart restores HardState/configuration and enters follower. Existing committed decisions remain valid across authority changes; old storage snapshots and term-independent application completion remain consumable, while entry-stability acknowledgment requires matching generation.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-election\",\n        \"B-transfer\",\n        \"B-io\",\n        \"B-recover\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-authority\",\n        \"F-config\",\n        \"F-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-abort\",\n        \"S-application\",\n        \"S-async\",\n        \"S-authority\",\n        \"S-auto-contract\",\n        \"S-caller\",\n        \"S-config\",\n        \"S-config-change\",\n        \"S-config-restore\",\n        \"S-dispatch\",\n        \"S-durable\",\n        \"S-election\",\n        \"S-follower\",\n        \"S-init\",\n        \"S-load\",\n        \"S-log-core\",\n        \"S-log-qualification\",\n        \"S-ready\",\n        \"S-ready-build\",\n        \"S-restore\",\n        \"S-send\",\n        \"S-storage\",\n        \"S-storage-resp\",\n        \"S-timeout\",\n        \"S-transfer\",\n        \"S-votes\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Applied membership determines support eligibility for both election and log commitment. Joint config requires both old and new majorities; recovery restores that same configuration, not a fresh quorum. Term reset clears votes and peer progress but retains committed history; log freshness and committed-prefix guards constrain subsequent formation. The new leader conservatively sets pendingConfIndex to inherited last index. Config proposals cannot overtake unapplied changes under normal validation. Automatic joint exit depends on application completion and leader role, and uses ordinary proposal admission, so an active transfer can reject it. Ordinary Ready completion only issues an apply acknowledgment for nonempty committed entries. readOnly support resets with authority, while pending pre-current-term reads have a distinct release path; their cross-context details remain open and their external API assigns retries to callers.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-config\",\n        \"B-auto\",\n        \"B-election\",\n        \"B-form\",\n        \"B-apply\",\n        \"B-client\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-config\",\n        \"F-applied\",\n        \"F-authority\",\n        \"F-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-advance\",\n        \"S-application\",\n        \"S-authority\",\n        \"S-auto-contract\",\n        \"S-caller\",\n        \"S-client-read\",\n        \"S-config\",\n        \"S-config-change\",\n        \"S-config-invariants\",\n        \"S-config-restore\",\n        \"S-dispatch\",\n        \"S-election\",\n        \"S-follower\",\n        \"S-init\",\n        \"S-joint\",\n        \"S-load\",\n        \"S-log-apply\",\n        \"S-log-core\",\n        \"S-log-pointers\",\n        \"S-log-qualification\",\n        \"S-majority\",\n        \"S-node-config\",\n        \"S-node-loop\",\n        \"S-proposal\",\n        \"S-read-queue\",\n        \"S-read-release\",\n        \"S-ready\",\n        \"S-replication\",\n        \"S-restore\",\n        \"S-timeout\",\n        \"S-tracker\",\n        \"S-transfer\",\n        \"S-votes\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Automatic exit after failed transfer with no new application completion.\",\n      \"Configuration-driven pending-read release and pendingReadIndexMessages across terms; caller retries constrain obligations.\",\n      \"Fine-grained asynchronous snapshot/application overlap and resource-error recovery.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Representative formation, authority, membership, persistence, rejection/retry, recovery and consumption paths are traced. Local questions remain; this map does not imply comprehensive safety or API coverage.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"be223e9a2bce49c